            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Rationalise the reciprocal using the sum of the two roots, then add.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Since $a>0$, both roots are real and $\\sqrt{a+1}>\\sqrt a$, so $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1x&=\\frac1{\\sqrt{a+1}-\\sqrt a}\\\\\\frac1x&=\\frac{\\sqrt{a+1}+\\sqrt a}{(a+1)-a}\\\\\\frac1x&=\\sqrt{a+1}+\\sqrt a\\\\x+\\frac1x&=(\\sqrt{a+1}-\\sqrt a)+(\\sqrt{a+1}+\\sqrt a)\\\\x+\\frac1x&=2\\sqrt{a+1}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
